# Docker / Podman Skills for Thesis Workload

## Container runtime: podman (macOS), Docker (Windows)

On macOS, `podman` is used instead of Docker. The `thesis` podman machine must be
running before any container operations:

```bash
podman machine start thesis
```

Set `DOCKER_HOST` so docker-compose and other tools work transparently:
```bash
export DOCKER_HOST=unix:///run/user/$(id -u)/podman/podman.sock
```

## Workload image

The workload container is defined in `src/Containerfile` (OCI-compatible, works with both
podman and Docker).

```bash
# Build (from repo root)
podman build -f src/Containerfile -t thesis-workload:latest src/

# Tag for local Kind registry
podman tag thesis-workload:latest localhost:5001/thesis-workload:latest

# Push to local registry (for Kind to pull)
podman push localhost:5001/thesis-workload:latest --tls-verify=false
```

The full build+push+deploy is automated via:
```bash
make k8s-deploy-dagster
```

## docker-compose (local dev stack)

The local development stack runs via `infrastructure/docker-compose.yml`:

```bash
make compose-up      # start postgres + dagster webserver + daemon
make compose-down    # stop
make compose-clean   # stop + remove volumes
```

Services:
- `postgres`: PostgreSQL 16 on port 5432
- `webserver`: Dagster webserver on port 3001
- `daemon`: Dagster daemon (run launcher)
- `workload`: gRPC server on port 4000 (thesis_workload job)

## Container image for K8s

The image pushed to `localhost:5001/thesis-workload:latest` is pulled by Kind cluster.
Kind is configured to trust the local registry via a ConfigMap in `kube-system`.

Registry contents:
```bash
curl http://localhost:5001/v2/_catalog    # list images
curl http://localhost:5001/v2/thesis-workload/tags/list   # list tags
```

## Containerfile notes

- Base: `python:3.12-slim` (keeps image small for quick pulls in Kind)
- Installs: `uv` + `dagster 1.12.7` + `dagster-k8s 1.12.7`
- Entry point: `dagster api grpc --host 0.0.0.0 --port 4000`
- Working dir: `/opt/thesis/workload`
- No root: runs as `dagster` user (UID 1000)
